«create_v6_refcon_test.ut
	«Creates v6 test artifact for refcon migration and 64-bit value widening
		«Purpose: Generate refcon_migration_test_v6.root database with:
			«  1. refconTests outline - various refcon values (including edge cases)
			«  2. longValueTests table - scalar long values (positive, negative, zero)
			«  3. refconDateTests outline - dates stored as refcon values
		«Usage:
			«  1. Import this script into Windows Frontier (v6.x)
			«  2. Run the script
			«  3. Copy resulting refcon_migration_test_v6.root to tests/fixtures/
		«Expected database structure:
			«refconTests (outline with 10 test cases, including nested children)
			«longValueTests (table with 8 scalar values + nested table)
			«refconDateTests (outline with dates as refcons for post-2038 testing)

local (dbPath = "C:\\Frontier\\refcon_migration_test_v6.root");

«Create new database
if not defined (@[dbPath]) {
	db.new(dbPath)};

«1. Create refconTests outline with all test cases
local (adrOutline = @[dbPath].refconTests);
new (outlineType, adrOutline);
target.set(adrOutline);

«Test Case 1: Zero refcon
op.insert("Test Case 1: Zero refcon", down);
op.setRefcon(0);

«Test Case 2: Positive small
op.insert("Test Case 2: Positive small", down);
op.setRefcon(42);

«Test Case 3: Positive large (near 2^31)
op.insert("Test Case 3: Positive large (near 2^31)", down);
op.setRefcon(2147483647);

«Test Case 4: Negative small
op.insert("Test Case 4: Negative small", down);
op.setRefcon(-123);

«Test Case 5: Negative large (min 32-bit)
op.insert("Test Case 5: Negative large (min 32-bit)", down);
op.setRefcon(infinity + 1);

«Test Case 6: Positive medium
op.insert("Test Case 6: Positive medium", down);
op.setRefcon(1000000);

«Test Case 7: Negative medium
op.insert("Test Case 7: Negative medium", down);
op.setRefcon(-1000000);

«Test Case 8: Nil refcon (not set)
op.insert("Test Case 8: Nil refcon (not set)", down);
«Intentionally DO NOT set refcon - leave uninitialized

«Test Case 9: Nested outline with children
op.insert("Test Case 9: Nested outline", down);
op.setRefcon(999);

«Add children to Test Case 9
op.insert("Child 1", right);
op.setRefcon(111);

op.insert("Child 2", down);
op.setRefcon(222);

«Return to parent level
op.go(left, 1);

«Test Case 10: Multiple levels (3-level hierarchy)
op.insert("Test Case 10: Multiple levels", down);
op.setRefcon(100);

«Level 2 child
op.insert("Level 2", right);
op.setRefcon(200);

«Level 3 grandchild
op.insert("Level 3", right);
op.setRefcon(300);

«Return to root level (go left twice)
op.go(left, 2);

«2. Create longValueTests table with scalar long values
local (adrTable = @[dbPath].longValueTests);
new (tableType, adrTable);

«Set scalar values
adrTable^.zeroLong = 0;
adrTable^.positiveSmall = 42;
adrTable^.positiveLarge = 2147483647;
adrTable^.negativeSmall = -123;
adrTable^.negativeLarge = infinity + 1;
adrTable^.positiveMedium = 1000000;
adrTable^.negativeMedium = -1000000;

«Create nested table with long values
local (adrNested = @[dbPath].longValueTests.nestedTable);
new (tableType, adrNested);
adrNested^.innerPositive = 999999;
adrNested^.innerNegative = -999999;

«3. Create refconDateTests outline with dates stored AS refcon values
local (adrDateOutline = @[dbPath].refconDateTests);
new (outlineType, adrDateOutline);
target.set(adrDateOutline);

«Date 2030 (post-2038 Y2038K test)
op.insert("Date 2030", down);
op.setRefcon(date.set(2030, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0));

«Date 2037 (near Y2038K boundary - Dec 31, 2037 23:59:59)
op.insert("Date 2037", down);
op.setRefcon(date.set(2037, 12, 31, 23, 59, 59));

return (true)
